<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/regranting-arrangement> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A Philanthropic Arrangement in which an organization receives funds and redistributes them to other organizations, acting as both a Grantee to the original source and a Funder or Funding Intermediary to the recipients." .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/regranting-arrangement> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/category> "funding-structure" .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/regranting-arrangement> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/legalNote> "Regranting to organizations without their own tax-exempt status (or across borders) can trigger expenditure-responsibility or equivalency-determination requirements under U.S. tax law. This ontology does not model those compliance steps." .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/relations/actsOnBehalfOf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/relations/actsOnBehalfOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A Fiscal Sponsor stands in for a Grantee that lacks independent legal status to receive an Award directly." .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/relations/actsOnBehalfOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/fiscal-sponsor> .
